{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "49", "x": 0.9036148555787364, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03012839302489931, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "The Amazonian manatee is the smallest species, though it is still a big animal. It", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.8258810763848841, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "grows to about 2.5 metres long and 350 kilogrammes. Amazonian manatees", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.826142104917271, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "favour calm, shallow waters that are above 23°C. This species is found in fresh", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.8262926115494565, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "water in the Amazon Basin in Brazil, as well as in Colombia, Ecuador and Peru.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.790541750057901, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "All three manatee species are endangered or at a heightened risk of extinction.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8261642503072929, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "The African manatee and Amazonian manatee are both listed as Vulnerable by the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.8265558956308273, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN). It is estimated that 140,000.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.8262295587028666, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Amazonian manatees were killed between 1935 and 1954 for their meat, fat and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.32139637352567824, "w": 0.8260989419117193, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "skin, with the latter used to make leather. In more recent years, African manatee", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3497267990426009, "w": 0.8267424910467521, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "decline has been tied to incidental capture in fishing nets and hunting. Manatee", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3780571491167385, "w": 0.8260772066215126, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "hunting is now illegal in every country the African species is found in.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40638753691226864, "w": 0.7048734877953783, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "The two subspecies of West Indian manatee are listed as Endangered by the IUCN.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4347178869864063, "w": 0.8260117957009852, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Both are also expected to undergo a decline of 20% over the next 40 years. A", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4630482747819364, "w": 0.8260238936455341, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "review of almost 1,800 cases of entanglement in fishing nets and of plastic", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.49140337008956114, "w": 0.8257504595937367, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "consumption among marine mammals in US waters from 2009 to 2020 found that", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5197337201636988, "w": 0.8262949696233941, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "at least 700 cases involved manatees. The chief cause of death in Florida", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5480641079592289, "w": 0.8264393247583512, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "manatees is boat strikes. However, laws in certain parts of Florida now limit boat", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5763944580333665, "w": 0.825837503279517, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "speeds during winter, allowing slow-moving manatees more time to respond.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6047248458288966, "w": 0.7830835722933694, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}